148CS c  2020Wu04 compiled for XUNDL database by B. Singh (McMaster)            
148CS c  2020Wu04: {+148}Cs nuclide produced at the RIBF-RIKEN facility in      
148CS2c  {+9}Be({+238}U,F) reaction at E=345 MeV/nucleon and an intensity of    
148CS3c  5pnA. Identification of fission fragments of interest was made based on
148CS4c  time-of-flight (tof), magnetic rigidity (B|r), and energy loss (|DE)   
148CS5c  using the BigRIPS spectrometer, determining atomic Z and mass-to-charge
148CS6c  ratio A/Q, where Q=charge state of the ions. The separated nuclei      
148CS7c  were implanted at a rate of 100 ions/s in the beta counting system     
148CS8c  of the Wide range Active Silicon-Strip Stopper Array for Beta and      
148CS9c  ion detection (WAS3ABi), which included a stack of five Double Sided   
148CSAc  Silicon Strip Detectors (DSSSDs). The WAS3ABi setup was surrounded     
148CSBc  by Euroball RIken Cluster Array (EURICA) array of 84 HPGe detectors    
148CSCc  for |g detection. Half-life of the separated and implanted ions        
148CSDc  was determined by fitting the time distribution of |b(implants)- and/or
148CSEc  |b|g(implants)-correlated decay curves to the sum of activities of     
148CSFc  parent nuclei, daughter nuclei, grand-daughter nuclei, |b-delayed      
148CSGc  neutron daughter and grand-daughter nuclei, and a constant background. 
148CSHc  Comparison of measured half-lives with FRDM+QRPA (2003), FRDM+QRPA     
148CSIc  (2019), KTUY+GT2, RHB+pn-RQRPA, and DF+CQRPA theoretical calculations. 
148CS c  2015OdZZ, 2015YaZW (same group): measured isomer T{-1/2}=4.2 |ms {I2}  
