148BA c  2018Li06: {+148}Cs produced through U(p,X) reaction with E(p)=1.4 GeV  
148BA2c  beam on UC{-x} target at ISOLDE-CERN. Measured yield, E|g, I|g,        
148BA3c  |b|g-coin, |g|g-coin. Also measured half-life of {+148}Cs g.s. from    
148BA4c  |g-decay curves using plastic scintillation detectors for |b particles,
148BA5c  LaBr{-3}(Ce) and HPGe clover detectors for |g detection. Measured      
148BA6c  %|b{+-}n=38 {I4} (from the ratio between the total number of {+147}Ba  
148BA7c  and {+148}Ba nuclei deduced from absolute intensities of 15.3% {I16}   
148BA8c  for the 167.4-keV |g and 6.7% {I7} for the 196.1-keV |g in {+147}La in 
148BA9c  |b{+-}n decay of {+148}Ba). Theoretical calculations with conserving   
148BAac  configuration mixing (SCCM) model. Comparison with {+146}Ba.           
