148CE c  2021Wa42 compiled for XUNDL database by E.A. McCutchan (NNDC) and N.   
148CE2c  Nica (Texas A&M)                                                       
148CE c  2020Ur03 compiled for XUNDL database by E.A. McCutchan (NNDC)          
148CE c  This reaction and level scheme was studied multiple times by same      
148CE2c  group as shown in the various publications listed below.               
148CE c  2021Wa42: measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, |g|g|g, |g|g|g|g, |g|g(|q) using    
148CE2c  Gammasphere array of 101 Compton suppressed Ge detectors. Extended     
148CE2c  2006Ch24 level scheme on simplex octupole band structures. Added       
148CE2c  |b and |g vibrational bands.                                           
148CE c  2020Ur03: measured precise E|g values for transitions from the levels  
148CE2c  8+ to 6+, 6+ to 4+, 4+ to 2+ and 2+ to 0+ gs, respectively             
148CE c  2006Ch24: measured E|g, I|g, |g|g using Gammasphere array of 102       
148CE2c  Compton suppressed Ge detectors. Deduced octupole correlations.        
148CE2c  Gave the most complete level scheme.                                   
148CE c  1971Ch44: measured I(|g+ce)                                            
148CE c  1995Ha20,1995ZhZV,1998ZhZH,1999HaZV: measured E|g, I|g,                
148CE2c  |g|gx-ray, |gX-ray, |g|g(|q), |g|g|g(|q)                               
148CE c  2009Go09: measured g-factor of the first 2+ state by the method of     
148CE2c  correlation attenuations in randomly oriented magnetic fields,         
148CE2c  or Integral Perturbed Angular Correlation technique (IPAC),            
148CE2c  using the Gammasphere array.                                           
148CE c  1999Sm05: measured g-factor of the first 2+ state using time-integral  
148CE2c  perturbed angular correlation method                                   
148CE c  See also: measured |g, |g|g, K| x ray                                  
148CE2c  (1995Zh39,1988Ph02,1970Wi16,1970Wa05,1971Ho29,1972Ho08,1974ClZX),      
