148PR    148CE B- DECAY                2004KO05,1983AR15,1997GR0926NDS    202601
148PR  H TYP=FUL$AUT=N. NICA$CIT=NDS 208, 1 (2026)$CUT=17-Jan-2026$             
148PR dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 23-Apr-2025)          
148PR c  2004Ko05: {+148}Ce produced by on-line spectrometer KUR-ISOL following 
148PR2c  the {+235}U(n,F) E=thermal reaction, implanted in tape and transported 
148PR2c  periodically to the measuring location equipped with three Si(Li)      
148PR2c  detectors, HPGe, and plastic scintillator detectors. Measured ce       
148PR2c  (FWHM=1.8 eV at 258 keV), |g, |b-gated ce and |g, ce-|g coin, T{-1/2}. 
148PR c  1997Gr09,1996Gr20: total absorption |g-ray spectrometer (TAGS) system  
148PR2c  located at INEL ISOL facility                                          
148PR2c  consisting of a 25.4 cm diameter, 30.5 cm long NaI(Tl) scintillation   
148PR2c  detector with a 20.3 cm deep axial well,                               
148PR2c  used to measure |b{+-} decay intensities, and the g.s. |b{+-} feeding  
148PR3c  when operated in the 4|p|g-|b coin mode                                
148PR c  1983Ar15: {+148}Ce produced by on-line spectrometer TRISTAN            
148PR2c  the {+235}U(n,F) E=thermal reaction, implanted in tape and transported 
148PR2c  periodically to the measuring location equipped with three Ge detectors
148PR2c  and a curved crystal spectromenter. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin,      
148PR2c  and T{-1/2}.                                                           
148PR c  Also measured: |g, |g|g, K| x ray (1977Bj02,1974Ar25,1973SeYX),        
148PR2c  |b|g (1978St03,1981Eb01), |g (1979Bo26), see 1986BuZV                  
148PR c  Level scheme is that of 1983Ar15. TAGS data with a number of           
148PR2c  pseudolevels with a substantial |b{+-} feeding to them indicates that  
148PR3c  the level scheme has large uncertainties associated with it and is     
148PR3c  incomplete.                                                            
148PR cB $TAGS data with a number of pseudo levels with a substantial |b{+-}    
148PR3cB feeding to them indicates that the level scheme has large              
148PR3cB uncertainties associated with it and is incomplete, due to which       
148PR3cB the I|b{+-} and log| {Ift} values are rather limits and                
148PR3cB listed with no uncertainties.                                          
148PR cB $When the calculated feeding overlaps zero within three standard       
148PR2cB deviations, the code GTOL (previous to the GLSC code)                  
148PR2cB calculates estimated upper limits (90% confidence level) which are     
148PR2cB given by evaluator in the table comments (see                          
148PR2cB "Statistics for Nuclear and Particle Physics", Louis Lyons,            
148PR2cB Cambridge University Press, 1986)                                      
148PR cB IB        From I(|g+ce) imbalances at each level, unless indicated     
148PR2cB otherwise. In computing I(|g+ce), 1983Ar15 assumed that |g's from      
148PR3cB E(level)<380 keV were M1, and |g's from E(level)>380 keV were E1 in    
148PR4cB general. The evaluator has changed these assumed multipolarities to be 
148PRxcB consistent with |DJ|p.                                                 
148PR cB IB$TAGS analysis gives the following pseudolevels and associated       
148PR2cB I|b (in %) in addition to the discrete levels listed. 880 keV 1.56;    
148PR3cB 970 keV 1.15-2.29; 1060 keV 0.73; 1150 keV 2.35;                       
148PR4cB 1260 keV|<1.33; 1360 keV 0.31; and 1430 keV 0.57.                      
148PR4cB The TAGS spectrum of {+148}Ce 56s decay,                               
148PR5cB while predominantly {+148}Ce, is estimated to contain <10% contribution
148PR6cB from {+148}Pr 2.0 min decay. A simultaneous analysis of both these     
148PR7cB nuclides was done, and the authors feel that in the energy range from  
148PR8cB |?750 keV to |?1300 keV, there is some ambiguity in the final results  
148PR9cB because of overlapping peaks. Since the resolution of the TAGS system  
148PRAcB is typically 50-100 keV, the intensity assigned to a pseudolevel may   
148PRBcB represent |b{+-} feeding to a single level or a group of levels. The   
148PRCcB same limitation applies to the intensity assigned to a known level,    
148PRDcB since it could include feeding to known or unknown levels in the       
148PREcB resolution energy range.                                               
148PR cB E(A)      |SI|b over g.s. and first four excited states is 0.0% {I21}  
148PR2cB from TAGS analysis (1997Gr09)                                          
