148ND c  1988Ka14: radioactive source from {+235}U(n,F), E=th at the TRIGA      
148ND2c  Mainz reactor using HELIOS ion separator. Used tape transport and      
148ND2c  measured E{-|g}, I{-|g}, |g|g-coin, |g|g(|q), with |b-gated |g         
148ND2c  multiscaling measurements. Used 3 Ge(Li) detectors for |g|g-coin       
148ND2c  (2.3, 1.9, and 1.8 keV FWHM at 1332 keV) and 2 Ge(Li) detectors for    
148ND2c  |g|g(|q) (1.9 keV FWHM at 1332 keV for both).                          
148ND2c  Deduced levels, J, |p.                                                 
148ND c  1997Gr09,1996Gr20: total absorption |g-ray spectrometer (TAGS) system  
148ND2c  used to measure |b-decay intensities, and the g.s. |b{+-} feeding when 
148ND3c  operated in the 4|p|g-|b coin mode                                     
148ND c  Measured: |g, |g|g                                                     
148ND2c  (1988Ka14,1986Wa06,1986BuZV,1979Ta17,1979Ik06,1979Bo26,1977Re11,       
148ND3c  \1977Bj02,1976Ya06,1976Sk04) |g|g(|q) (1988Ka14,1979Ik06), |b, |b|g    
148NDxc  (1986Gr11,1979Ik06,1978St03,1976LoZT)                                  
148ND c  Level scheme is that of 1988Ka14. TAGS data  from 1997Gr09 with a      
148ND2c  number of pseudolevels with |?25% |b{+-} feeding to them indicates     
148ND2c  that the level scheme is not complete and has large uncertainties      
148ND4c  associated with it.                                                    
148ND cB $Due to the large uncertainties associated with the pseudo levels      
148ND3cB and the incompleteness of the level scheme, the I|b{+-} and log| {Ift} 
148ND3cB values are rather limits and listed with no unceratinties              
148ND cB IB        From I(|g+ce) imbalance at each level, unless indicated      
148ND2cB otherwise.                                                             
148ND cB IB$TAGS analysis gives the following pseudolevels and associated       
148ND2cB I|b (in %) in addition to the discrete levels listed. 2650 keV 1.18;   
148ND3cB 2750 keV 1.39; 2850 keV 0.80; 3200 keV 0.70; 3300 keV 0.80;            
148ND4cB 3400 keV 1.39; 3500 keV 1.61; 3600 keV 0.86; 3700 keV 0.75;            
148ND5cB 3800 keV 1.29; 3900 keV 2.04; 4000 keV 4.82; 4100 keV 4.50;            
148ND6cB 4200 keV 1.82; 4300 keV 0.96; 4400 keV 0.32;                           
148ND7cB 4500 keV 0.064; 4600 keV 0.032; 4700 keV 0.011. The TAGS               
148ND8cB spectrum is                                                            
148ND9cB estimated to have |?1.5% uncorrected contamination of {+148}Pr(2.0     
148NDAcB min). Since the resolution of the TAGS system is typically 50-100 keV, 
148NDBcB the intensity assigned to a pseudolevel may represent |b{+-} feeding to
148NDCcB a single level or a group of levels. The same limitation applies to    
148NDDcB the intensity assigned to a known level, since it could include        
148NDEcB feeding to known or unknown levels in the resolution energy range.     
