148ND  H TYP=FUL$AUT=N. NICA$CIT=NDS 208, 1 (2026)$CUT=17-Jan-2026$             
148ND c  Measured: |g, |g|g (1979Ik06,1986Wa06,1984Ch30,1976Ya06); %|b{+-} of   
148ND2c  the parent (2004Ko05,2008KoZO)                                         
148ND c  1997Gr09,1996Gr20: total absorption |g-ray spectrometer (TAGS) system  
148ND2c  used to measure |b{+-} decay intensities, and the g.s. |b{+-} feeding  
148ND3c  when operated in the 4|p|g-|b coin mode                                
148ND c  Level scheme is that of 1979Ik06 with some modifications indicated by  
148ND2c  1986Wa06 and 1982DeYW. TAGS data with a number of pseudolevels with    
148ND3c  |?69% |b{+-} feeding to them indicates that the level scheme is not    
148ND4c  complete and has large uncertainties associated with it.               
148ND cB $Due to large uncertainties associated with the level scheme and its   
148ND3cB incompleteness, the I|b{+-} and log| {Ift} values are rather limits    
148ND3cB and listed with no unceratinties                                       
148ND cB $|b-feeding was determined assuming no ground-state |b decay           
148ND cB IB        From I(|g+ce) balance at each level                          
148ND cB IB$TAGS analysis gives the following pseudolevels and associated       
148ND2cB I|b (in %) in addition to the discrete levels listed. 1600 keV 0.9;    
148ND3cB 1950 keV 1.6; 2050 keV 2.7; 2150 keV 2.1;                              
148ND4cB 2250 keV 2.1; 2400 keV 20.3; 2500 keV 5.2;                             
148ND5cB 2600 keV 1.2; 2700 keV 1.7; 2800 keV 3.5; 2900 keV 3.6;                
148ND6cB 3000 keV 1.3; 3100 keV 1.0; 3200 keV 1.9; 3300 keV 1.9;                
148ND7cB 3400 keV 1.6; 3500 keV 0.6;                                            
148ND7cB 3600 keV 0.6; 3700 keV 1.0; 3800 keV 1.3; 3900 keV 3.0;                
148ND8cB 4000 keV 3.0; 4100 keV 3.0; 4200 keV 0.6; 4300 keV 1.3;                
148ND9cB 4400 keV 0.6; 4500 keV 0.3;                                            
148NDxcB 4600 keV 0.16. A simultaneous analysis of the spectra of both {+148}Ce 
148NDacB and {+148}Pr 2.0 min decay was done, and the authors feel that in the  
148NDbcB energy range from |?750 keV to |?1300 keV, there is some ambiguity     
148NDccB in the final results because of overlapping peaks. TAGS analysis       
148NDdcB indicates that transitions to the pseudolevels above 1859 keV account  
148NDecB for |?68% of |b{+-} intensity in this decay. Since the resolution of   
148NDJcB the TAGS system is typically 50-100 keV,                               
148NDFcB the intensity assigned to a pseudolevel may represent |b{+-} feeding   
148NDFcB to a single level or a group of levels. The same limitation            
148NDGcB applies to the intensity assigned to a known level, since it could     
148NDHcB include feeding to known or unknown levels in the resolution energy    
148NDIcB range.                                                                 
148ND cG           For some gammas part of the observed I|g may belong to       
148ND2cG 2.29-min {+148}Pr |b{+-} decay                                         
148ND cG           For possible additional |g's see {+148}Pr |b{+-} decay (2.29 
