148EU cL $Configurations given by 1981Pi10 (IT decay and (p,3n|g) datasets) and 
148EU2cL 1995Jo04 (({+13}C,4n|g) dataset). They are of the                      
148EU2cL multi-ph type, characteristic for nuclei with fewer valence nucleons   
148EU2cL which are spherical or weakly oblate deformed                          
148EU cG E,RI$For normal deformation data, from the IT decay dataset from g.s.  
148EU2cG up to and including the 720 isomer, from the ({+13}C,4n|g) dataset     
148EU3cG above up to and including the 6703 level, and from ({+27}Al,|a5n|g)    
148EU3cG above, except where noted. From the ({+29}Si,p4n|g):SD dataset for the 
148EU4cG superdeformed data.                                                    
148EU cG M$Based on |a(K)exp from {+148}Eu IT decay and (p,3n|g); and |g(|q),   
148EU2cG DCO, linear polarization, |a(K)exp data from ({+13}C,4n|g)             
148EU cG MR(Y)$Estimated from |a(K)exp data in ({+13}C,4n|g)                    
148EU cG MR(Z)$Not given by authors in ({+13}C,4n|g)                            
148EU cG RI(A)$Relative intensities within the SD-1 band, normalized to |?1     
148EU2cG for the strongest transition in the mid-energy region of the band      
148EU cL E$From least-squares fit to E|g's with limited uncertainties avalable  
148EU2cL for the E|g input. When no unceratinties are given the E(level)        
148EU2cL values are calculated with the assumption that the uncertainties are   
148EU2cL the same (of 0.3 keV) for all the E|g's                                
