148GD d  Dataset revised March 15, 93 by B. Singh to include SD band data from  
148GD2d  1993Ha19 and 1988De10. Revised and updated November 1995 to include dat
148GD3d  on SD bands from 1995DeZZ and 1996Sa15. Updated mar 4, 96 to include SD
148GD4d  band data from 1996De04. Updated (B. Singh) May 1997 to include SD band
148GD5d  data from 1997Zh03 and 1997Ha19. Updated (B.SINGH) May 1998 to include 
148GD6d  SD bands from 1998By02.                                                
148GD c  Other reactions:                                                       
148GD2c  1991Fl03: spin dependence of GDR in Gd isotopes                        
148GD c  There are problems in reconciling log| {Ift} values from {+148}Tb |e   
148GD2c  decay (2.20 min) with |DJ|p of the transitions. More data are needed   
148GD3c  to clarify these problems.                                             
148GD cG E         From |e decay, (HI,xn|g), and (HI,xn|g):SD                   
148GD cG M         Except where noted otherwise, mult assignments are based     
148GD2cG on conversion electron and |g(|q) of oriented nuclei from |e decay     
148GD3cG (60 min), conversion electron data from |e decay (2.20 min), |g|g (|q),
148GD4cG excitation function, conversion electron and |g|g(|q) data from        
148GD5cG (HI,xn|g).                                                             
148GD cG RI        Relative photon branching from each level for gammas from    
148GD2cG normal deformed states as opposed to relative intensity within each SD 
148GD3cG band                                                                   
148GD cG RI(a)$Branching ratio from (HI,xn|g) (2000Po13)                        
148GD cG RI(A)$Relative intensity within each SD band, normalized to            
148GD2cG |?1 for the most intense transition in that band                       
148GD cG E(S)      |g not reported by 1996De04                                  
148GD cG E(U),RI(U)$From 1996De04 only                                          
148GD cG E(V)$From 1995DeZZ. |g not reported by 1996De04 and 1997Ha19           
148GD cL E$From a least-squares fit to E|g data with |DE|g=1 keV for E|g's with 
148GD2cL no assigned uncertainty                                                
148GD cL J$Except where noted otherwise, J|p assignments are based on           
148GD2cL conversion electron and |g(|q) of oriented nuclei from |e decay        
148GD3cL (60 min), conversion electron data from |e decay (2.20 min), and       
148GD4cL |g|g(|q), excitation function, conversion electron and |g|g(|q) data   
148GD5cL from (HI,xn|g), with J values generally increasing with excitation     
148GD5cL energy for the latter dataset. Starting at 7274 level and above the    
148GD5cL normal deformation data are exclusively from (HI,xn|g) (1990Dr06) with 
148GD5cL parity assumed by the authors based on theoretical and                 
148GD5cL level scheme arguments and tacitly adopted as tentative by the         
148GD6cL evaluator.                                                             
148GD cL J$Band designations for normal deformed states are from (HI,xn|g)      
148GD7cL (1990Pi17).                                                            
148GD7cL Except for the ground state (g.s.) band, the other medium-to-high      
148GD2cL excitation sequences can be classified as single-particle sequences    
148GD3cL rather than collective bands. This is due to the fact that, having only
148GD4cL two valence neutrons over the Z=64, N=82 doubly magic shell, such a    
148GD5cL nucleus typically starts at smaller oblate deformations and develops   
148GD6cL shape coexistence in the normal deformation regime. At very high       
148GD7cL excitation energies, it develops very large prolate, superdeformed     
148GD8cL shapes with corresponding collective rotational superdeformed bands.   
148GD9cL For uniformity, the evaluator kept the conventional designation of     
148GDacL bands for all sequences.                                               
148GD cL T         From (HI,xn|g), unless indicated otherwise                   
148GD CL BAND(P)$|n{+2} states.                                                 
148GD CL BAND(Q)$|n{+2} x octupole states                                       
148GD CL BAND(R)$|n{+2} x |p{++1}|p{+-1} states                                 
148GD CL BAND(S)$|n{+2} x |p{+2} states                                         
148GD CL BAND(T)$|n{+2}|p{+2} x octupole states                                 
148GD CL BAND(A)$SD-1 band (1995DeZZ,1993Ha19,1988De10). Configuration=|p6{+2}  
148GD2cL |n(7{+1}1/2[651],|a=-1/2) (1998By02). Q(intrinsic)=14.6 {I2}           
148GD3cL (1996Sa15). Percent population=1.6 {I1} (1996De04), 1.30 {I15}         
148GD4cL (1993Ha19), 0.72 {I25} (1997Zh03) in {+124}Sn({+29}Si,5n|g) E=157 MeV  
148GD5cL (1996De04,1997Zh03), E=155 MeV (1993Ha19). Other values from 1992Fl02: 
148GD6cL 1.9 {I5} in {+76}Ge({+76}Ge,4n|g); 0.8 {I2} in {+124}Sn({+29}Si,5n|g)  
148GD7cL and 0.5 {I2} in {+122}Sn({+30}Si,4n|g).                                
148GD CL BAND(B)$SD-2 band (1995DeZZ,1993Ha19,1996De04). Configuration=|p6{+2}  
148GD2cL |n(7{+1}1/2[651],|a=+1/2) (1998By02). Promotion of neutron from        
148GD3cL 1/2[651],|a=-1/2 to 1/2[651],|a=+1/2. Q(intrinsic)=14.8 {I3}           
148GD4cL (1996Sa15). Percent population=0.7 {I2} (1996De04), 0.62 {I20}         
148GD5cL (1993Ha19).                                                            
148GD CL BAND(D)$SD-3 band (1995DeZZ,1996De04). This band reveals a backbend at 
148GD2cL a rotational frequency of |?0.72 MeV. configuration=|p6{+2}            
148GD3cL |n((1/2[651],|a=-1/2)(1/2[651],|a=+1/2)) (1998By02). Promotion of      
148GD4cL neutron from 1/2[770],|a=-1/2 to 1/2[651],|a=+1/2. Q(intrinsic)=17.8   
148GD5cL {I13} (1996Sa15). Percent population=0.4 {I2} (1996De04), 18% {I3} of  
148GD6cL SD-1 (1995DeZZ).                                                       
148GD CL BAND(E)$SD-4 band (1995DeZZ,1996De04). Configuration=|p6{+2}           
148GD2cL |n(7{+1}(1/2[651],|a=-1/2)(1/2[651],|a=+1/2)) (1998By02). Promotion of 
148GD3cL neutron from 5/2[642],|a=+1/2 to 1/2[651],|a=+1/2. Percent             
148GD4cL population=0.5 {I2} (1996De04), 12% {I4} of SD-1 band (1995DeZZ).      
148GD CL BAND(F)$SD-5 band (1995DeZZ,1996De04).                                 
148GD2cL configuration=|p(6{+4}1/2[301]{+-2}) |n(7{+2}(1/2[651],|a=-1/2)        
148GD3cL (1/2[651],|a=+1/2)) (1998By02). This involves promotion of two neutrons
148GD4cL from 1/2[411] to 7{+1} and 1/2[651],|a=+1/2 orbitals. Or               
148GD5cL configuration=|p(6{+2}(1/2[301],|a=-1/2){+-1}(3/2[651],|a=+1/2))       
148GD6cL |n(7{+1}1/2[651],|a=-1/2) (1998By02). This band is identical (in       
148GD7cL transition energies) to {+152}Dy SD-1 band. Percent population=0.5 {I1}
148GD8cL (1996De04), 23% {I4} of SD-1 band (1995DeZZ).                          
148GD CL BAND(G)$SD-6 band (1995DeZZ,1996De04,1997Ha19). Configuration=|p6{+2}  
148GD2cL |n(7{+1}(1/2[651],|a=-1/2)(1/2[651],|a=+1/2)) (1998By02). Promotion of 
148GD3cL neutron from 1/2[411],|a=+1/2 to 1/2[651],|a=+1/2. 1997Ha19 provide    
148GD4cL evidence for |DJ=2 staggering of 0.37 keV {I12}, and propose that this 
148GD5cL band is identical to {+149}Gd SD-1, yrast band. Percent population=0.4 
148GD6cL {I1} (1996De04), 16% {I3} of SD-1 band (1995DeZZ).                     
148GD CL BAND(H)$SD-7 band (1998By02).  configuration=|p6{+2} |n(7{+1}(5/2[402] 
148GD2cL or 9/2[514])) (1998By02). Promotion of neutron from 1/2[651],|a=-1/2 to
148GD3cL 5/2[402] or 9/2[514]. Bands SD-7 and SD-8 are probably signature       
148GD4cL partners. Percent population=5-10% of SD-1 band (1998By02)             
148GD CL BAND(J)$SD-8 band (1998By02). Configuration=|p6{+2} |n(7{+1}(5/2[402]  
148GD2cL or 9/2[514])) (1998By02). Promotion of neutron from 1/2[651],|a=-1/2 to
148GD3cL 5/2[402] or 9/2[514]. Bands SD-7 and SD-8 are probably signature       
148GD4cL partners. Percent population=5-10% of SD-1 band (1998By02)             
148GD CL BAND(K)$SD-9 band (1998By02). Percent population=5-10% of SD-1 band    
148GD2cL (1998By02)                                                             
