148GD    (HI,XNG):SD                   1998BY02,1996DE04,1995DEZZ26NDS    202601
148GD  H TYP=FUL$AUT=N. NICA$CIT=NDS 208, 1 (2026)$CUT=17-Jan-2026$             
148GD d  Dataset created (B. Singh) March 1993 to include SD bands from 1993Ha19
148GD2d  and 1988De10. Updated (B. Singh) November 1995 to include data from    
148GD3d  1995DeZZ and 1996Sa15. Updated (B. Singh) March 1996 to include data   
148GD4d  from 1996De04. Updated (B. Singh) May 1997 to include data from        
148GD5d  1997Zh03 and 1997Ha19. Updated (B. Singh) May 1998 to include data from
148GD6d  1998By02                                                               
148GD c  1998By02: {+124}Sn({+30}Si,6n|g) E=158 MeV. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g|g  
148GD2c  using EUROGAM array of 54 Compton-suppressed Ge detectors. Three new   
148GD3c  SD bands reported                                                      
148GD c  1996De04: {+124}Sn({+29}Si,5n|g) E=157 MeV. Discrete |g-ray data for   
148GD2c  6-SD bands obtained with GASP array (40 Compton-suppressed Ge          
148GD3c  detectors and 80 BGO detectors)                                        
148GD c  1995DeZZ: {+124}Sn({+30}Si,6n|g). Discrete |g-ray data for 6-SD bands  
148GD2c  obtained from higher-fold |g-ray coincidence data using the            
148GD3c  EUROGAM array consisting of 54 Compton-suppressed Ge detectors         
148GD c  1996Sa15 (see also 2001Cl05): {+124}Sn({+30}Si,6n|g) E=158 MeV.        
148GD2c  Measured lifetimes and deduced Q for SD-1, SD-2, SD-3 bands, using the 
148GD2c  EUROGAM array consisting of 54 Compton-suppressed Ge detectors         
148GD c  1997Zh03: study of feeding mechanism of SD bands through               
148GD2c  observation of continuum |g rays feeding normal and superdeformed      
148GD2c  states, using GASP array, yrast-SD band reported                       
148GD c  1997Ha19: {+124}Sn({+29}Si,5n|g) E=158 MeV. Deduced six SD bands,      
148GD2c  evidence for |DJ=2 staggering for SD-6 band                            
148GD c  1993Ha19: {+124}Sn({+30}Si,5n|g) E=155 MeV                             
148GD c  1992Fl02: {+124}Sn({+30}Si,5n|g) E=155 MeV, {+122}Sn({+30}Si,4n|g)     
148GD c  1988Dr01: {+116}Cd({+36}S,4n|g) E=170 MeV                              
148GD c  1988De10: {+124}Sn({+30}Si,5n|g) E=155 MeV and {+104}Ru({+48}Ca,4n|g)  
148GDxc  E=215 MeV                                                              
148GD cG           Two additional SD bands are reported by 1998By02 with the    
148GD2cG following |g-ray cascades. The assignment to {+148}Gd is not firm.     
148GD3cG The first band (u1) is similar to SD-9 band in the moment of inertia   
148GD4cG plot with E|g's close to the midpoint energies of SD-9 band. The       
148GD5cG second band (u2) has transition energies close to 3/4 point energies   
148GD6cG of SD-2 band, but the moment plots show differences.                   
